    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_first_degree_core_one_quadratic_gap_four_double_root_separated_heavy_row_correction_exact_order",
    "title": "A=1 quadratic separated heavy-row correction exact order",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "exact correction-root valuations and coprimality of the overlap polynomial",
    "statement": "On the squarefree supported-disjoint separated double-root locus, at each correction root tau the fixed heavy row has exact order 2-ord_tau Lambda, equal to the order of H=g_*S_B^2/J. This follows because X-x_* has normalized-curve order three, the Forney section has order two, and the Pade syzygy subtracts exactly one at a center; replacing the moving curve point by x_* changes the value only in order at least three. Hence the free overlap polynomial T_j is nonzero at both correction roots and gcd(T_j,S_B)=1.",
